# sync_timedb Parsing Collapse Vectorization

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

Multi-`dev` metric collapse in ingest parse (`_collapse_stats_with_deltas` and helpers) must use the fastest available vectorized path. Per-group `groupby.apply` is a known ~50× regression on GPU ingest workloads. The same hot-path discipline applies to **counter/arc carry state** and **streaming resume**.

## Forbidden

- `DataFrame.groupby(...).apply(...)` for multi-`dev` metric collapse in the ingest parse path.
- Parallel collapse logic in `sync_timedb.py` — all routes go through `_collapse_stats_with_deltas`.
- Carry-state loops of the form `for key, group in groupby(...): last = group.iloc[-1]` or `first_rows.iterrows()` + `.at[...]` / per-row `index.get_loc` in `_apply_counter_deltas` / `_apply_arc_and_finalize` (RC-4; production py-spy hit in `fast_xs` / `find_common_type`).
- Streaming resume that fast-forwards with bare `fd.readline()` without feeding skipped lines through the parser (RC-0; empty `schema` silently drops every hardware stats line).
- Per-event `dict` / `{**rec}` / `DataFrame.from_records` on the hardware emit hot path — compile `!` schema once and append columnar lists.
- Extra pandas `.copy()` / `.astype(str)` / object-string `groupby` when native `sum(min_count=1)`, integer/category keys, or unix seconds until ORM suffice.
- Re-parsing `W=`/`U=` schema tokens on every value token.
- Per-line `zip(*compiled)` in `_append_compiled_stats_columns` — compiled schema must be parallel arrays (`events` / `wids` / `mults` / `units`) extended directly.
- `cols["value"].extend(float(v) for v in vals)` generator extend — materialize `[float(v) for v in vals]` once then extend.
- Prefilling every `HOST_PROC_KEYS` entry to `None` on each proc sample — sparse rows omit missing keys; `@fast` slow keys stay absent (never invent 0).
- `build_stats_dataframes` round-trip `DataFrame` → `to_dict(orient="records")` → peak-merge → `DataFrame` — peak-merge the proc list, then one frame.
- Calling `schema_key_basename` on every proc sample — compile bare names at `!` into `schema_bare` / `schema_fast_bare`.
- Decoding ASCII under `_stats_file_read_lock` on rb streaming readers — use `_read_stats_line_batch_decode_after_lock` (bytes under SH, `_decode_stats_readline` after release).
- Adding Polars, PyArrow, or numba as runtime parse engines before a logged host/pipeline flamegraph shows leftover exclusive time in `feed_line` / `split` / `float`.
- Shipping a Cython `.so` by default; dual-ABI bake is required if a later gate still shows ASCII split/float as the bottleneck.

## Required — use the fastest available method

| Collapse need | Required approach |
|---------------|-------------------|
| Sum across devs (`min_count=1`) | `_groupby_sum_min_count` |
| **GPU types** (`nvidia_gpu` / `amd_gpu` / `intel_gpu`) | Collapse group cols **include `dev`** (`_COLLAPSE_GROUP_COLS_WITH_DEV`) — keep per-device rows; sum/mean/max/OR only within a device. Non-GPU types keep `_COLLAPSE_GROUP_COLS` (no `dev`) and set `dev=''` on output. |
| Event-dispatched standard reducers (sum/max/mean) | Partition by event class → `groupby.agg` with native reducers |
| Bitwise OR (`clocks_event_reasons`) | `_nvidia_bitwise_or_values` (`numpy.bitwise_or.reduce`) on OR slice only |
| Custom reducer (DCGM cluster-mean, dynamic gap) | `_collapse_dcg_cpu_power_vectorized` — explicit `for key, group in grouped` + NumPy `_cluster_mean_sum_sorted` (`reduceat`), **not** `apply` |
| New metric type / event class | Extend typed router in `_collapse_stats_with_deltas`; add equivalence test vs apply reference |
| Last-row-per-group **carry** (`carry.raw` / `carry.arc`) | `groupby(...).tail(1)` + array extract into packed tuples (`(value, wid, mult, time)` / arc unix seconds) — **never** `group.iloc[-1]` per group or per-row inner dicts |
| First-row carry application | Index-aligned / mapped assignment (`.loc[...]` once) — **never** `iterrows()` + `.at[...]` or per-row `index.get_loc` |
| Streaming resume offset | Feed every line from offset 0 through `feed_line` / `feed_lines`; gate emission with parser `start_idx` (same as `parse_stats_lines`). Physical `readline` skip is forbidden. |

Arc continuity (`_ARC_GROUP_COLS`) includes ``dev`` so multi-GPU rates stay per-device. Node-level summary plots still sum across devices in ``get_aggregate_df``.

## Resume state integrity (RC-0)

Any parse that resumes at a mid-file line index must accumulate schema/state from the prefix. Reference: `parse_stats_lines` feeds all lines and gates only the digit-timestamp branch on `i >= start_idx`. Streaming entry points (`parse_stats_file_streaming`, `parse_stats_file_streaming_incremental`) must match that contract. Callers must **not** `lines[start_idx:]` then parse with `start_idx=0` — that drops the `!` schema on small-file payload resume.

## Carry deltas: one wrap and one scale

`_apply_counter_deltas` carry assignment stores **unscaled** `value - prev`. Wrap (`wid`) and `* mult` run once on the full delta column. Carry deltas are **unscaled** until that single wrap + `* mult`. Scaling inside the carry loop double-applies `mult` (legacy `U=64B` MBW/CAS) on chunked ingest and listend.

## DCGM blanks in cluster-mean

`_cluster_mean_sum_sorted` must nan-out DCGM blanks (`nan_out_dcgm_numeric_blanks`) before the finite filter. A `2**47` blank is missing telemetry, not a ~1.4e14 W cluster.

## Payload parsed row counts

Payload meta (`_parse_stats_file_payload_impl` / `_parse_stats_file_payload_impl_streaming`) must set `stats_rows_parsed` from `stats_payload_row_count` **before** collapse. Zero-host marks use parsed counts, not post-collapse `stats_rows`. Do not change the incremental combined path, which already accumulates parsed counts.

## Sample-header ``jid`` on host_data

Digit-line jobid belongs on stats ``tags`` (same value as proc ``tags2``). Collapse helpers preserve ``jid`` with ``"first"`` when the column is present (`_optional_jid_first_agg`); do **not** add ``jid`` to ``_COLLAPSE_GROUP_COLS*`` (DB uniqueness stays time/host/type/event[/dev]). Empty delta frames include ``jid``. ORM maps ``"-"`` → NULL.

## Canonical helpers (`sync_timedb_parsing.py`)

- `_collapse_stats_with_deltas` — single entrypoint
- `_groupby_sum_min_count` — rest + NVIDIA sum/default slices
- `_collapse_nvidia_gpu_vectorized` — NVIDIA event-class native aggregations
- `_collapse_dcg_cpu_power_vectorized` — DCGM explicit group loop
- `_collapse_nvidia_gpu_group` / `_collapse_dcg_cpu_power_gauge_group` — apply-reference only (tests)
- `_apply_counter_deltas` / `_apply_arc_and_finalize` — vectorized carry continuity for incremental flush; carry deltas unscaled until wrap + `* mult`; keep unix seconds until `to_pydatetime_or_none`
- `_compile_schema_tokens` — SoA (`events`/`wids`/`mults`/`units`); `_append_compiled_stats_columns` extends without `zip(*compiled)`
- `_compile_schema_bare_names` / `schema_bare` — proc basenames compiled at `!`
- `_read_stats_line_batch_decode_after_lock` — rb batch under SH; decode after release
- `IncrementalStatsParser` — compiled schema SoA + columnar `_stats_cols`; `take_stats_columns()` for production flushes; `parse_stats_lines` records adapter for tests
- `stats_payload_row_count` — zero-host marks use parsed row counts, not post-collapse lengths

